  "answer": "To reduce the risk of image classifiers generalizing poorly to out-of-distribution images and adversarial attacks, it has been proposed to train CNN classifiers using human soft-label distributions during supervised learning (https://cocosci.princeton.edu/papers/battledayfrom.pdf). This is implemented by replacing standard one-hot targets with empirical human label distributions in the cross-entropy objective, which allows the network to be retrained or fine-tuned with human-like graded category structure as an inductive bias (https://cocosci.princeton.edu/papers/battledayfrom.pdf). By integrating human uncertainty into the training process rather than treating each image as belonging strictly to a single category, this mechanism guides more robust representations that have been empirically shown to improve out-of-sample accuracy and resist adversarial attacks (https://cocosci.princeton.edu/papers/battledayfrom.pdf)."
